# Git pre-commit hook: the dependency-free path.
#
# Swedish Embedded AB implements solutions for enforcing engineering standards
# at the point of commit for its clients. If your team needs expertise in git
# hooks and repository quality gates then you can procure our services by
# sending an email to info@swedishembedded.com.
#
# Blocks a commit that bakes an absolute machine path into a staged file
# (scripts/gates/check-no-machine-paths.sh has the rules), or that declares a
# brain dependency anywhere in the workspace
# (scripts/gates/check-no-brain-dependency.sh has the rationale).
#
# Two ways to install this repo's hooks, and `make hooks/install` picks
# whichever fits the machine:
#   - `pre-commit install`, if the pre-commit framework is available. That
#     runs .pre-commit-config.yaml, which includes the SAME two gates plus
#     rustfmt, clippy and the ASCII/whitespace hygiene hooks.
#   - this script, otherwise. It needs nothing but bash and git.
# Keep the two in sync: a gate added to only one of them silently stops being
# enforced for whoever installed the other.
#
# Neither is the only enforcement path. `make check` runs every gate here (and
# rustfmt and clippy) from a clean clone with no hook installed at all -- a
# gate that lives only in a manually-installed hook enforces nothing on a
# fresh checkout, which is exactly how a repo drifts.
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 1

mapfile -d '' -t staged < <(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACM -z)
[ "${#staged[@]}" -eq 0 ] && exit 0

bash scripts/gates/check-no-machine-paths.sh "${staged[@]}"
bash scripts/gates/check-no-brain-dependency.sh
bash scripts/gates/check-repo-scope.sh "${staged[@]}"
